vpinos-core (1.1.32) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Setup has a new item, VPinFE 3.0 Beta, for trying the VPinFE 3.0
    beta before it's released. Join installs the newest beta, and Update
    VPinOS then keeps the cabinet on the newest beta and moves it to
    VPinFE 3.0 when that's released. Leave goes back to VPinFE 2.x. It
    needs internet, works on amd64 and arm64, and on the live USB it's
    lost on reboot. Boot on startup moves to item 8.
  * VPinFE 3.0 converts its settings to a new file on its first start,
    and keeps the old one, so Leave brings back the settings from before
    the beta. VPinOS Configuration now writes VPinFE's screens to
    whichever file the installed VPinFE uses.
  * VPinFE 3.0 names its windows differently. Saving in VPinOS
    Configuration now updates the cabinet's screen rules so VPinFE's
    windows reach the right screens with either version. After joining
    the beta on a cabinet with more than one screen, open VPinOS
    Configuration and Save once.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:44:46 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.31) trixie; urgency=medium

  * With an NVIDIA driver (NVIDIA proprietary or NVIDIA legacy), the menu
    no longer drops to a low resolution after a program exits. The
    computer's built-in startup display was left running beside the
    NVIDIA driver, and the menu treated it as an extra screen and shrank
    to fit it. VPinOS now turns it off once the NVIDIA driver is loaded.
    The other text consoles (Ctrl+Alt+F2 and up) are blank with these
    drivers. The Default driver is unchanged.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:19:32 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.30) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Ready for Visual Pinball 10.9, which keeps its settings in a new
    folder, ~/.local/share/VPinballX/10.9 instead of 10.8. VPinOS
    Configuration and the VR on/off switch now use the folder of the
    Visual Pinball version that's installed, so they keep working before
    and after the update. The first time 10.9 runs, it copies the 10.8
    settings into its new folder. VPinOS Configuration no longer creates
    the folder itself, which would have stopped that copy.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:54:01 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.29) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Testing has a new item, DOF Test: a table for testing DirectOutput
    Framework (DOF) toys one at a time. The flipper buttons step through
    DOF events E901 to E990, only the selected one is on, and the
    backglass shows its number. It isn't installed by default: the first
    time it's picked, the menu offers to install it (about 8 MB, needs
    internet). On the live session, VPinFE and SSH Password
    Authentication move to 4 and 5 in Testing.

